I have an old and battered copy of
the 78032 user's guide (this is
for the chip itself ... I'm still
looking for the KA630 user guide!).

SAVISP saves the ISP at the time
a chip restart occurs.

SAVPC saves the PC.

SAVPSL saves the following:
	<07:00> - PSW
	<14:08> - restart code
	<15:15> - MAPEN bit
	<31:16> - PSL<31:16>

These get filled in when any of the following happen:
	- RESET is asserted
	- HALT is asserted (i.e. halt button pressed)
	- HALT instruction is executed with chip in kernel mode
	- severe hardware or kernel software corruption occurs

The manual states that these registers must
be saved before reenbaling the MMU or using
any emulated instructions.

The rest of the system state at this time
is:

 SP     = SP at time of restart
 PSL    = 0x041F0000
 PC     = 0x20040000
 MAPEN  = 0
 ICCS   = 0
 SISR   = 0
 ASTLVL = 4
 everything else is undefined

Antonio

