You may need to set up the environment within cron to be similar to
your interactive. Run .profile (Bourne or Korn) or .cshrc (C-Shell)
first and then set the output variables. Best to put it all together
in a script. e.g.

in Bourne
#!/bin/sh

. .profile

TERM=""; export TERM
<unset other interactive variables>
run prog

in C-Shell
#!/bin/csh

source .login
source .cshrc

unset TERM
<unset other interactive variables>
run prog

Hope this helps,

Chris Bullivant


