Maintenance Manual, which is pretty good, tho not up to the quality
and detail of later manuals.

http://www4.service.digital.com/documentation/pcdoc/celxl5.htm

Next, if you have a Celebris XL 5xxx, the motherboard should be a DEC
part number 54-23606-01 or -02, I forget exactly which.  No matter.
An lower part number is not capable of running dual processors.

The Celebris XL was designed to run up to 166MHz dual Pentium (classic
only) or a single 200Mhz.  I have all the parts needed to do so,
except I am out of 200Mhz CPUs and pretty short on 166s right now.
But I do have some inventory of the latest and best processor card,
54-24490, if you need, and the voltage regulator module required for
faster Pentium processors.

