Actually, most compilers don't have to optimize for the P4 to see grreat
speed improvements, they just have to optimize in such a way as to not
create roadblocks for execution on P4.  VC7 creates code that, while not
optimized for P4 runs without penalties for instance.  Also, the recent SP5
processor pack upgrades for VC6 do the same.





