the X 72  memory is ECC. Non-ECC memory is X 64.

Standard PC100 stuff works fine in my 164SX. (Micron 128Meg sticks -
CT16M64S4D8E .... you need 2 as the SX needs memory in pairs). The SX will
accept the 256M version too (CT32M64S4D8E). The 128M sticks are single
sided & the 256M sticks are double sided. Previous generation 128M sticks
were double sided & work too.

If you want ECC, the Micron parts are CT16M72S4D8E or CT32M72S4D8E.

Other manufacturers likely work fine too, but I'm happy with Micron
(www.crucial.com) so that's what I can suggest works in the 164SX.

HTH.

EM

