In article <3B859A6F.9F714AC1@dgf.uchile.cl>, Super-User <rodrigo@dgf.uchile.cl> writes:
> Dear all
> Does exist a way to limit the cpu usage for users or process ?

On VMS for per-user limits use the command:

	MCR AUTHORIZE MODIFY <username>/CPUTIME=<whatever>

On VMS for per-process limits, modify your $CREPRC call to specify
the PQL$_CPULM quota.

There are corresponding methods from DCL and when setting up Batch queues.


