> Ok so I bought a PC 164SX motherboard and cpu, now the question is what
> type of ram is best? After reading some previous postings some people
> claim that nn X 72 (8,16,32) works best. But ECC or non ECC? Any known
> brands that work well? Any help appreciated.

nn X 72 = ECC
nn X 64 = non-ECC

The SX can use either ECC or non-ECC RAM (in fact, I'm typing this
message on an SX with a pair of 256 MB ECC modules, but I used to run
with non-ECC).  To my knowledge, the SX is the only alpha board which
allows one to use either ECC or non-ECC RAM modules.

Do not mix ECC and non-ECC modules, though.

As far as brands go, I have had no problems with the Viking ECC
modules I have now.  The Micron PC66 non-ECC RAM I had before that
also worked just fine.

The following thread may be of use to you:

http://www.lib.uaa.alaska.edu/axp-list/archive/1999-04/index.html#547

Hope that helps and enjoy your board!
Craig


