sam.

on the as255, the on board scsi connector is 50pin, not 80pin (aka SCA).

it's a ribbon cable that supports upto 3 internal drives plus a scsi cdrom
or tape.  the 255 normally shipped (at least in later models) with a 7200rpm
seagate 2G barracuda under the cdrom unit.  you can then add a 1.6" and 1"
