Until recently only TOPS-10 has been able to boot under the publicly
available emulators but now TOPS-20 V4.1 boots (with some caveats)
under Bob Supniks simh emulatos for the PDP-10 (KS10 DECSYSTEM-2020).
Index 

It's all still preliminary and there are some bugs but both it and
(possibly) ts10 (another simulator) have finally reached the stage
where they can boot TOPS-20. They've been able to boot TOPS-10 for
some time but TOPS-20 required more floating point support. I actually
had tears in my eyes when I saw "System restarting, wait..." The last
time I saw that  was in 1990 with the "SYSTEM OVERRIDE" switch toggled
to override failing fans just to boot one last time before it was
wheeled out the door.

Most of the old DECUS tapes are online and available for download so
we can start programming in Simula again :)

Some of the info needed is all over the place but a good start point
is
 http://www.aracnet.com/~healyzh/pdp10emu.html and the alt.sys.pdp10
newsgroup.

Just in the last week or so pre-built binaies have been made availble
for WIndows and the emulator claims to be able to compile and run
under VMS but I haven't tried that yet.
--
Alan


