> I haven't done any real benchmarks but on a 500 Mhz Pentium III things
> look at least as fast as a real 2020 (the baby of the PDP-10 family)
> and a 2020 was around 1/5th speed of a KL10 from distant memory (I
> last used a 2020 in 1985). So the 2020 was comparable to a VAX 11/780
> (or maybe 750)
>
Though it has been quite a few years (1977), my first systems programmer
job was on a 2020.  It could handle up to 8 COBOL interactive
programmers working at the same time but slowed dramatically on the 9th
programmer.  Our benchmarks on overnight batch processing of COBOL
financial apps showed it to be slightly faster than our IBM 370/138 (was
there a 138 model?  that's the one that sticks in my decaying memory)
running VM.

From my strictly personal observations not founded on any kind of test
the 2020 felt faster than a 11/750 at the keyboard using COBOL, FMS and
DBMS).  DBMS on a VAX was a speed killer, more so than the 20.
  Jack Peacock




