Actually, we called the TK50 and the TZ30 DLT.

The next generation we called DLT II, then DLT III and then DLT IV.

The technology was all Digital Linear Tape, and it was a evolutionary
process going from 95MB to over 80GB compressed.

The tape drive head design is very important, but in fact, the actual tape
itself and it's chemical formulation is the most important aspect to getting
such high density without having to go to helical scan systems.

Once again, DIGITAL designed a top technology.

rtt

