I've seen several systems become hung due to problems with memory. 
Although high IPL can be the culprit, just plain bad memory or a CPU /
motherboard related problem can be fatal.  By bad memory I mean a failure
that hangs the memory bus and not just a few memory locations that are bad. 
You can't execute the dump or console code in that case.

You might try the system exerciser with

>>> set auto_action halt
>>> init
>>> sys_exer

Let it run for a while then

>>> show_status

>>> kill_diags
>>> cat el


