> There is only 6 megabytes of memory installed, what kind of memory
> fits? This thingie doesn't use SIMM -modules?

According to the T 50 output, you have:

	MicroVAX 2000
	6MB RAM
	(2) RD54 (190MB unformatted, 159MB formatted)

The ? DZ error is warning.  You are using a serial console, so that
serial port can not be tested.

The ? TPC error is a warning that nothing was seen on the bus.  The MV
is at ID 7.  Don't use that ID.

The ?? NI error is because your ethernet is not terminated.  Either
terminate it or connect it to a network.  If you have a MV2K with both
AUI and Thinwire connectors, make sure that the switch is set to select
the correct interface.

Since you mention a SCSI ID switch, I assume that the tape drive you
have is a TK50Z-GA.  The -FA model did not have a switch.  Set the
switch to ID 1.  Connect a cable from the MV2K to the TK50Z (either
connector) and put a terminator on the other connector on the TK50Z.

The vast majority of MV2Ks are either 4MB or 6MB.  There is 2MB on the
motherboard.  Most expansion cards are 2MB or 4MB.  There is a 12MB card
available.  It is a MS400-CA.  This gives you a 14MB system.

Alternately, Clearpoint made a memory card that took you up to 16MB (the
maximum addressable by the CPU chip).  IIRC, this card required custom
ROMs, so make sure that you get the ROMs if you find one of these cards.

Good luck!

