The VAXstation 3100 series all use the 
same 68-pin connector.

The VAXstation 4000 series all use the
same 50-pin connector.

My recollection is that all the 
MicroVAX 3100 series use the 50-pin
connector.

There is a more recent connector (with
even more pins, but I've not counted them)
on the latest SW stuff.

You can find a set of pinouts at:
http://www.hardwarebook.net/connector/index.html#Storage

The 50-pin connector is (AFAIK) the same
everywhere. The main complaint about the
DEC 68-pin one is that they used the
different gender to everyone else - 
although it always looked the other way
round to me :-)

