The 3rd (rightmost) bay has two removable plastic rails on the sides,
which narrow it down for a normal SBB.  The "backplane" in this bay can
also be taken out and reinstalled farther back, to make room for a deeper
device like a CD or 4mm tape drive.  To make either of these adjustments,
you have to take the cover off.

At least some of the CD drives used a metal mounting bracket and a small
internal cable for the SCSI and power connection.  I've seen the bracket,
but not a mounted drive.  I don't know if these drives were in SBBs, or
mounted "by hand".


The BA353 was shipped in various configurations, with different part
number suffixes.  I don't know if the plastic rails for the 3rd bay were
orderable separately.

