    I solved the first part of the problem ( thanks to the CSC ).

    To force a halt on a PWS you have to remove the cover. On the system
board at the same level as the top DIMM connector and to the rear of
the system is a small momentary action push button. Pushing this in
will get you the >>> at which point you can type CRASH to get a crash
dump.

    As to why it hung in the first place, that is still an open question.



