Cthulhu wrote:
> 
> Hoff Hoffman <hoffman@xdelta.zko.dec.nospam> wrote:
> 
> >  Alternatively, the CPU model code -- usually KA* -- is normally displayed
> >  when the system powers up and runs its diagnostics, and the various KA*
> >  codes for the various processors are listed in the OpenVMS FAQ.  Post it.
> 
> So now, what is the difference between the Model 30 and the Model 40? :)

If you mean the VAxstation 3100 Model 30 and the
VAxstation 3100 Model 40, then the answer is
only the box. The main logic board is identical
between the two. The Model 40 is a slightly
taller case that can accomodate an
extra set of disk drives internally.
My recollection is that it also has
a larger PSU.

Similarly the VAXstation 3100 Models 38 and 48
differ only in the boxes in which they are
found.

The MicroVAX 3100 Models 10 and 20 are identical
(apart from case size ...) as are the 10e and 20e.
The MicroVAX 3100 Models 30 and 40 are identical
too.

Antonio

