>At Wed, 1 Aug 2001 00:03:41 -0400, "Martin" <pcguru01@bellsouth.net> claimed:

>    I am looking for the dos cdrom drivers for the decpcxl 590 any help
>would be greatly appreciated.

Assuming {as Ben also wrote} you have a scsi-cd
connecting to the NCR53C810 scsi-host, you need,
aspi8xx.sys
symcd.sys
mscdex.exe   { should be in your DOS directory }

sample,

config.sys
device=C:\<path_to>\aspi8xx.sys
device=C:\<path_to>\symcd.sys /D:ASPICD0

autoexec.bat
C:\DOS\mscdex.exe /D:ASPICD0 /M:12

The comment ASPICD0 can be changed to whatever
suits you, just make sure it's the same in both lines.

This posting is also mailed to "Martin".
In case you have to mail me back Martin, change the 
.@cybercity.dk to bsd AT pobox.dk as the replyto: is invalid.
Please do let me know if you need/would like to be mailed the drivers.

>TIA,
>martin

