You can still download the Service Maintenance Manual for the Venturis
FX at:

http://www4.service.digital.com/documentation/pcdoc/venfx.htm

If you replace the "shorting block" in the voltage regulator socket
next to the processor with the right voltage regulator, (and do the
right switch settings) you can certainly install and run a Pentium MMX
at 233MHz.  This is slightly beyond the original design of the
motherboard, but the design was fairly open ended with the
Intel-standard voltage regulator socket.

I still have nearly 2 trays of 233Mhz Pentium MMX pulls available,
plus cooling fans and voltage regulator modules, if you're interested
in buying.  Mail from here to there is fairly reasonable for small
packages.

I'm a little dubious about running an AMD K6-2 at 400MHz in this
board, altho I have voltage regulators that will step down the voltage
to the 2.2v required by the AMD.  I have done this with the later
Venturis FX-2.

Cyrix CPUs are definitely out.  They are not worth the trouble.  They
run HOT HOT HOT, and are not too stable... Ben Myers

